// D1443 — an ANONYMOUS struct literal whose field holds a LIST OF ANONYMOUS STRUCTS,
// delivered everywhere. The annotated face spells the destination `{ f: {g: f64}[] }` and
// runs; the un-annotated face leaves inference to pin it, and the mint had no field code for
// a struct-ref list, so the OUTER literal got no row at all. The rescue was a `type`
// DECLARATION of the OUTER shape — not the element, not the element list — so this template
// must never declare one, or every cell goes green for the wrong reason.
//
// The PROOF discriminates rather than just building: it reads THROUGH the list element
// (`v.f[0].g`), so a row whose element heap type came from the wrong shape would trap or
// print the wrong number rather than pass.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
// @@VALUE@@
{ f: [{ g: 1.5 }] }
// @@TYPE@@
{ f: {g: f64}[] }
// @@PROOF@@
print(v.f[0].g)
// @@WANT@@
1.5
// @@VALUE2@@
{ f: [{ g: 2.5 }] }
// @@TYPE2@@
{ f: {g: f64}[] }
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v.f[0].g + 1.0)
// @@WANT2@@
3.5
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a struct, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
